Original commit body from 7c55d2865ed4a022ed234a263c8e8f2000991c78:

WI-napaf gave a receiverless call that resolves nowhere the external
placeholder; these sibling shapes stayed silent:

- untyped variable receiver (obj.write): external placeholder with
  call_construct=method, as js (WI-nasuf), python, java, go do;
- implicit-self sends parsed as a bare identifier (current_user,
  params, puts), also as a call receiver or a [] object: told from a
  local read by Ruby's own lexical rule (_is_ruby_local: a parameter,
  block parameter, rescue / for variable or earlier assignment in the
  scope; a block's bindings visible only inside it), which replaces the
  parameters-only guard (and its now-unused helper);
- self.m(...): binds the enclosing class's own method;
- a name 3+ classes define (AMB-METHOD) and super / super(...): an
  unresolved edge with enclosing_class (the superclass for super) for
  the inherited-calls linker, the owner as module, never "external"
  (WI-napaf's rule: the name is the project's); K#go -> Base#go now
  resolves through the linker;
- direct recursion: the self edge, as python and java emit it.

